.TH SAPHIRA-BOOTSTRAP 8 "September 2026" "Saphira Linux" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
saphira-bootstrap \- install a Saphira profile into an empty directory
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B saphira-bootstrap
.RB [ \-r
.IR REPOSITORY ]
.I TARGET
.RI [ PROFILE ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B saphira-bootstrap
assembles a Saphira root filesystem by installing an install
.IR profile (5)
into
.IR TARGET .
It copies the host repository keys, writes the repository
configuration, and runs
.B apk --root
.I TARGET
.B --initdb add
with the profile's package list.
.PP
.I TARGET
must be an existing, empty directory (a
.I lost+found
entry is tolerated for fresh filesystems).
.B saphira-bootstrap
requires root privileges: it creates device nodes' mount points and
must own the resulting tree.
.PP
.I PROFILE
defaults to
.BR base .
Any profile file present under the profile root is accepted; names
are restricted to letters, digits, dot, underscore, plus and hyphen
so a profile name can never escape the profile directory.
Profile references are expanded recursively with cycle detection,
and duplicate packages are installed once.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-repository =\fIREPOSITORY
Use
.I REPOSITORY
as the APK repository for the target instead of copying
.IR /etc/apk/repositories .
.TP
.I TARGET
Empty directory that receives the new system. Aborts unless
.I TARGET/bin/sh
is executable and
.I TARGET/usr/lib/libc.so
exists after installation. The installer itself provides the root
shell convention
.RI ( /bin/sh
as a link to
.BR bash ,
and
.I /usr/bin/env
as a link to
.IR /bin/env ),
mirroring the package builder's root initialization; no package owns
those links.
.TP
.I PROFILE
Profile name as described in
.BR saphira-profiles (5).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SAPHIRA_REPOSITORY
Same effect as
.BR \-r .
.TP
.B SAPHIRA_PROFILE_ROOT
Directory holding profile files (default
.IR /usr/share/saphira/profiles ).
.TP
.B SAPHIRA_APK
APK binary to invoke (default
.BR apk ).
.TP
.B SAPHIRA_ID
.BR id (1)
binary used for the root check (default
.BR id ).
.TP
.B SAPHIRA_BOOTSTRAP_PLAN
When set to
.BR 1 ,
print the profile name, repository and the exact
.B apk
invocation that would run, then exit without touching
.IR TARGET .
No privileges are needed in plan mode.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The profile installed and the sanity checks passed.
.TP
.B 1
Any failure: not root, target missing or non-empty, unknown or
invalid profile, profile cycle, no repository keys, APK error, or a
target without a usable
.IR /bin/sh .
.TP
.B 2
Usage error.
.SH EXAMPLES
Print what
.B virtualisation-host
would install, without privilege:
.PP
.RS
SAPHIRA_PROFILE_ROOT=./profiles SAPHIRA_BOOTSTRAP_PLAN=1 \\
    saphira-bootstrap /tmp/rootfs virtualisation-host
.RE
.PP
Install the base profile from the live repositories:
.PP
.RS
sudo saphira-bootstrap /mnt/saphira
.RE
.PP
Install the virtualisation host from a pinned repository:
.PP
.RS
sudo saphira-bootstrap \-r /out/stage4/packages/hatched/x86_64 \\
    /mnt/saphira virtualisation-host
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/saphira/profiles/
Profile definitions; see
.BR saphira-profiles (5).
.TP
.I TARGET/etc/apk/repositories
Repository configuration written into the new system.
.TP
.I TARGET/etc/apk/keys/
Repository public keys copied from the host.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR saphira-profiles (5),
.BR saphira-chroot (8),
.BR saphira-genfstab (8),
.BR apk (8)
